# tasks.mf — Marketak remaining-v1 work plan

Machine-readable project plan. Markdown per the owner-agreed format (phase
headers, stable T-ids, `Status:` fields instead of checkboxes).

## 0. Authority and constraints

The executing agent has **no database access**. Every data fact below was
verified live against project `erxxsebcqqcpkipzcdhg` (`marketak`,
`eu-central-1`, Postgres 17.11, `ACTIVE_HEALTHY`) during planning, or is
quoted from one of exactly three files. Nothing else is a source:

- Live database (verified 2026-10-10, read-only `SELECT`s): full `*_v1`
  RPC catalogue read — every RPC this plan calls exists with the
  documented args (`quote_order_v1`, `place_order_v1`, `cancel_order_v1`,
  cart ×2, addresses ×4, profile ×3, discovery ×2, full rider set, device
  token, flags, earnings); CHECK vocabularies match §4 exactly (orders 9,
  sub_orders 9, assignments 10, payment 4, settlement 4, rider 4, vehicle
  4, channels, methods, `is_online` CHECK, totals formula); 13 `settings`
  keys exactly as listed; `authenticated`: riders SELECT=false, orders
  SELECT=true, addresses INSERT=false, notifications UPDATE=false; zero
  tables without RLS; `claim/mark_events_v1` are service_role-only while
  app RPCs grant `authenticated`; push routing returns exactly the 7
  documented rows; 19 template keys × ar/en. (`normalize_text_v1` also
  exists; no task uses it — observed, out of scope.)
- `specs-mobile/README.md` — the database contract. Wins every dispute
  about data. It is a transcription: the agent **never edits it**.
- `apps/mobile/README.md` — the mobile architecture contract (8 layers,
  7 rules, folder tree). Map over tree.
- `AGENTS.md` — the 11 standing rules, checklists A/B/C, commit protocol.
- `DESIGN.md` v2.0 ("Telemetry Dispatch Terminal", dark-only) — the
  interface contract AND the sole styling authority: frontmatter tokens
  are canonical and win over prose; feature code references tokens only,
  never raw hex or numbers, never an invented value; layout follows the
  measured window, never the device; courier terminal highest density
  56/48, customer medium 48; theme layer before screens (§15 RN overrides
  first); every screen exits through the §17 pre-ship checklist with
  unverified items listed. §18 defaults assumed + flagged (text wordmark
  icon; 30 s dispatch window; 8 km/h + 150 m; Western digits in telemetry,
  locale digits in prose). DESIGN.md merchant-console and live-map
  sections are out of scope / out of v1 — never build from them.
- Owner directions (explicit, not repo-derived): the Tamagui + NativeWind
  + expo-image UI stack (§2, F-01/F-06); the agent never opens `supabase/migrations/`; no git
  history is consulted — files absent from the working tree are never
  authority.

Not sources: git history, `CHANGELOG.md` (removed by owner direction),
`decisions.md`, migration internals. Where this plan names a prior record,
it does so only to flag a required human sync — never as build authority.

- Living-record rule: with `CHANGELOG.md` removed, AGENTS.md rule 6
  (same-commit docs sync) still holds — each task's record goes to the
  repo's current living-docs location; if none exists, the task notes the
  record in its commit message and flags it under §5 Q3 instead of
  inventing a file.
- `specs-mobile/README.md` §14 queries, P4 implementation, real-push
  observation, store-console actions, anything needing `SUPABASE_DB_URL`
  are **reviewer-side** (human with access), cited under `Verify (human)`.
  `check:policies` exits **2** without DB access: "unchecked", never "clean".

Out of scope: `apps/admin-web`, `apps/vendor-web`, `packages/ui`
(absent from the working tree — verified by directory read); live rider
tracking / map (§13, out of v1); any screen in §13's no-build list.

## 1. Task schema

Every task is a `### <ID>` block with exactly these fields:

- `Status:` — one of `pending | in_progress | blocked | in_review | done`.
  All start `pending`. `in_review` = agent work complete, needs human/DB
  verification. Only `done` unblocks dependents.
- `Depends on:` — stable IDs, `none`, or `P<n> exit` (whole phase gate).
- `Inputs:` — files/sections the agent must read first. DESIGN.md cites
  are section-precise (`DESIGN §9.2`, not "the design").
- `Outputs:` — deliverables (contract paths from `apps/mobile/README.md` §1).
- `Acceptance:` — verifiable, evidence-based criteria. UI tasks cite the
  quality bar (§1.1) plus task-specific points. No vague verbs.
- `Verify:` — repo commands. Never edited tests, never `.skip`/`.only`.
- `Risks:` — optional; known traps from the contracts.

Rules: IDs unique and stable. Every `Depends on` target exists. Graph is
acyclic. Priority never overrides a dependency. Tasks appending to the same
barrel file (`services/rpc/index.ts`, `packages/shared/src/index.ts`) are
explicitly sequenced, never parallel. `.gitkeep` is deleted the moment the
first real file lands in its folder (AGENTS.md rule 11).

### 1.1 UI quality bar (every task that ships a screen)

Derived from DESIGN.md §§2–9, 11–15 and AGENTS.md A4. A screen is not done
until all applicable lines hold; the §17 checklist is run per screen and
unverifiable items are listed, never silently passed.

- States: loading = square loader only (3×8px squares, 160 ms sequence;
  control width frozen, taps ignored, busy announced; reduced motion =
  static `LOADING` text — never a round spinner); error = server copy
  verbatim for business failures, input errors per DESIGN §9.6 (crimson
  border + glyph + `body-sm` row); empty = 32 glyph + heading stating what
  is empty + `body-md` next step + one action (§9.9); disabled primary
  always carries a one-line reason caption.
- Component states: default, pressed (feedback at 0 ms, ≥100 ms visible,
  rectangular — native ripples/highlights replaced per §15), focus-visible
  (2 px `focus-ring` + 2 px offset, never removed), disabled, loading,
  error, selected (4 px leading `cobalt-high-beam` bar + `surface-raster-2`).
- Type: tabular numerals everywhere (`fontVariant: tabular-nums`);
  amounts/codes/coords never truncated, never count-up animated; Arabic:
  no uppercase transform, `letterSpacing` 0, bundled fallback font (Space
  Grotesk / JetBrains Mono cover no Arabic — §3.2/§13.5), line heights
  rounded up to 4 px grid; bidi isolates (U+2066–U+2069) around IDs, codes,
  coords, amounts inside RTL text; OS scale to 150 % (`label-*` cap 130 %),
  rows/buttons `min-height` so text growth reflows.
- Layout from the live window (§4.1: verify at 360/600/840/1200 widths and
  375/900 heights): 56 primary / 48 secondary targets, 48 hit areas, 8 px
  gaps; primary action ≤480 wide, in-thumb-reach; resize/rotation preserves
  sheet snap, scroll, selection, form drafts; keyboard snaps sheet to full
  + action above IME; edge-to-edge with insets respected (bottom action
  padding = `max(inset,16)+8`); compact-height landscape goes side-by-side.
- Contrast from the §2.5 table, not judgment: no cobalt `#1D4ED8` as text/
  border/icon on dark; no text on high-beam fill; white text only on
  cobalt-electric; crimson text only on raster-0/1; control boundaries
  `wire-border-control` 0.40 (mid/dim are dividers, never control bounds);
  every state pairs color + glyph + text label (§2.3).
- Icons: Material Symbols Sharp only (never Rounded), courier `wght` 600 /
  customer 400, FILL 1 when active, 20/24 (32 empty states only); RTL
  mirrors arrows/chevrons/`keyboard_double_arrow_right`, never `navigation`,
  clocks, checks, barcodes; shipped in-binary, never fetched (§7).
- Motion tokens only (§8 durations + linear/standard easing); reduced
  motion removes pulses/sweeps, swaps slides for instant changes; no
  springs, no parallax, no auto-carousels.
- Accessibility (§12): accessible name matches visible text; reading order
  = visual order; live ETAs `polite`, throttled (≤ every 30 s or ≥1 min
  change); offers/emergency/breach `assertive`; every drag/long-press/swipe
  has a tap alternative (slide rail → button + confirm dialog, §9.2);
  haptics/sound never the only feedback; focus order verified on tablets.
- Voice (§13.1–13.2): terse imperative, sentence-case body/labels,
  glossary (courier, customer, merchant, dispatch, order, pickup,
  drop-off, handoff, vertical) — "driver" never appears. Formats (§13.3):
  countdowns `MM:SS`, locale clock for arrival, one unit per screen,
  merchant currency tabular, trailing-aligned in tables.
- Imagery (§13.4): 4:3 menu / 1:1 grocery, `wire-border-dim`, unfiltered;
  missing photo = raster-1 block + `image` glyph; parcel = glyph, no photo.
- System states (§11): offline = cached content + age + writes disabled
  with reason; stale data shows `UPDATED xx AGO`, never stale ETA as live;
  unknown telemetry = `--`, never `0`.
- Privacy/safety (§14): pharmacy item names never in notifications, lock
  screens, switcher snapshots, or courier manifests (sealed-package copy);
  camera/location denied = manual path + settings-action empty state;
  permissions requested in context with a one-line why.
- Tests (AGENTS.md rule 4): every behaviour ships edge-case **and**
  failure-path tests — loading, error, empty, offline, denied-permission,
  RTL, 150 % scale, reduced motion, screen-reader labels. Suites are never
  weakened to pass.

### 1.2 Data quality bar (every task that touches the boundary)

Money fails closed (nonnegative ints, parse failure throws — never renders
`0`); unknown keys `.passthrough()`; first schema mismatch per RPC
recorded; error code parsed from the message head (PostgREST `code` is
always `P0001` per §9); client never prices, never judges eligibility,
never runs the state machine — it sends intent, renders the server's
answer, branches on codes (§1 of the db contract).

Verification commands (from root `package.json`, all verified present):

```
npm run typecheck   # tsc --build (+ workspaces)
npm run lint        # eslint .
npm test            # vitest run (packages/*, apps/* — NOT functions/*, see W-01)
npm run test:integrity                        # scripts/check-test-integrity.mjs
npm run check:secrets  npm run check:hardcoded-colors
npm run check:policies # needs SUPABASE_DB_URL; exit 2 = unchecked
npm run check:status-types
npm run verify      # all of the above in order
npm run deps:check  # from apps/mobile — the architecture gate
npm run align       # from apps/mobile — expo install --check (SDK 57 floor)
```

Coverage floors (`vitest.config.ts`, verified present): lines/functions/
statements 80, branches 70, over `packages/shared/src/**` +
`apps/mobile/src/services/**`.

## 2. Phases

| Phase | Objective | Entry | Exit |
|---|---|---|---|
| P0 Foundation | Toolchain, boundary layers, theme, session/role, icon+font delivery — nothing shippable, everything later depends on it | Contracts read (§0) | `deps:check` green with fixture proof recorded; `verify` green except documented `check:policies` exit-2 |
| P1 Customer slice | Specs-mobile §20 steps 1–9: browse → cart → address → quote → place → track → cancel | P0 exit | Full customer flow; P1-09 green; §17 checklists per screen recorded |
| P2 Rider slice | Specs-mobile §20 step 10: read-and-claim only; stop at §13 gaps | P1 exit (`apps/mobile/README.md` §11: one customer slice before any rider slice) | Claim → collect → deliver path green; missing-RPC screens absent, not stubbed |
| P3 Worker hardening | Suite integrity + worker notes evidenced in-tree | None (parallel-safe; touches only `functions/`, root config, living record) | Worker tests run in `npm test`; type note closed; manual-only validations documented as human |
| P4 Backend gaps | The 6 ranked §13 gaps that need new RPCs. Agent writes backend **requirements** to the living record for a human DB engineer; builds nothing against them; never touches migrations | P1 exit (gap surfaces are defined by slices) | Requirements recorded per §15 conventions; app surfaces stay absent by rule |
| P5 Launch gates | Evidenced device/infra gates (storage signer, APNs, Android SHA) | None (parallel-safe) | Each gate closed with evidence or recorded `blocked` with owner |
| P6 Store submission | App Store + Google Play readiness: build profiles, assets, listings, review prep | P1 exit; S-03 needs P5 closed | `eas.json` + assets + metadata in-tree and consistent; human console steps named with owners |

