  per `align`: `tamagui ^2.7.7`, `nativewind ^4.2.7` + `tailwindcss
  ^3.4.19`, `expo-image ~57.0.5`, `expo-notifications ~57.0.22`,
  `expo-auth-session ~57.0.14`, `expo-apple-authentication ~57.0.2`,
  `@react-native-firebase/{app,analytics,crashlytics} ^26.4.0`;
  pre-existing Expo pins confirmed SDK-current by `expo install --fix`,
  unchanged), `apps/mobile/app.json` (config plugins auto-added for
  expo-image + firebase at install — verify at implementation),
  metro/babel configs (compiler + utility wiring per the installers'
  documented Expo procedure)
- Outputs: `apps/mobile/package.json` (+ lockfile) with Tamagui
  (+ compiler config), NativeWind + tailwind config, `expo-image` +
  `src/theme/` (Tamagui dark theme from DESIGN tokens: radius 0 all
  sizes, colors/fonts; tailwind config mapped from the same frontmatter;
  ONE token source with a documented boundary — Tamagui theme owns kit
  components, utilities own layout/custom, no value lives in both;
  rectangular press states, square switch/checkbox/radio per §9.5, 2 px
  focus treatment); Space Grotesk 600/700 + JetBrains Mono 400/500/600/700
  + Arabic fallback font + Sharp icon set bundled (expo-font config);
  auth via system-mediated OAuth only (Google + Apple, no embedded
  credential entry — `npm run align` must pass); push-token module
  present for F-08. Custom-build boundary recorded: rail, signature,
  square loader, scanner overlay exist in no kit and are built per §9
  (F-06/R-04/R-05) — everything else comes   from the kit + utilities. Baseline recorded 2026-10-10: shared
  toolchain aligned to root (TS ~6.0.3, vitest ^5; duplicate installs
  pruned); root `dependency-cruiser` removed (no root consumer — mobile
  keeps its own); one TS6-surfaced lint fixed (`errors.ts` no-op
  assertion, rule-proven). Session record 2026-10-10: display-name
  locales (`assets/locales/ar|en.json`) restored so export works;
  `babel-preset-expo@~57.0.14` added as devDep (Metro could never resolve
  it — every prior bundle attempt was broken); Sharp icons resolved via
  `@expo-google-fonts/material-symbols-sharp@0.4.61` (8/8 fonts bundled,
  magic-verified); Metro `expo export` proof passed (2009 modules);
  token↔tailwind parity spot-checked identical; `react-native-web`
  correctly refused (ERESOLVE vs react 19.2.3; native Tamagui chain
  verified clean of it). Session record 2026-10-10 (boot proofs): live
  `expo start` runs caught two runtime-only Tamagui validations no gate
  can see — `space` gained `true: spacing.md`, `zIndex` became numeric
  slots 0–6 over token values (full dev-validation list read from
  Tamagui's bundle: size/space `true`, radius/zIndex overlap — all four
  now satisfied). Firebase loads behind a guarded `require` (Expo Go
  has no native modules; silent + one warn there, real in dev builds).
  Remaining: human dev-build render both platforms + airplane-mode icon
  check — unperformable until screens exist (C-01/R-01), so this task
  closes on first rendered screens, not before.
- Acceptance: `npm run align` passes (green at install 2026-10-10;
  re-verify after wiring); a planted rounded-default component fails the theme assertion —
  radius 0 proven, not assumed; compiler output verified on a dev build
  (human: both platforms render); theme and utilities never disagree
  (spot-check the same token through both paths); icon font renders the
  §7 courier glyph set offline (airplane-mode render check, human);
  Arabic glyphs render from the fallback, digits from JetBrains Mono
  (§13.5); no version hand-pinned against the SDK manifest
- Verify: `npm run align`, `npm run lint`, `npm test`
- Risks: two styling engines — the boundary doc is load-bearing, and any
  value living in both configs is a defect. Installed versions are listed
  in Inputs; re-verify with `align` after any bump; a version breaking
  SDK 57 agreement is rejected, not forced. The compiler adds build time
  — acceptable, recorded.

### F-02

- Status: done
- Title: Prove the dependency-cruiser rules fail for the right reasons
- Depends on: none
- Inputs: `apps/mobile/README.md` §4 (six fixtures),
  `apps/mobile/.dependency-cruiser.cjs` (verified present on disk)
- Outputs: Observed evidence 2026-10-10 (fixtures created, run, removed;
  tree green after). Of the six README-named violations exactly ONE fired:
  fixture 5 → `no-second-money-module`. Fixtures 1/4/6 (cross-zone,
  deep-rpc, shared-zone) produced nothing: their rules use `path.join`
  constants, which compile to backslash regexes that never match
  forward-slash cruised paths — the rules are inert on Windows (they work
  on POSIX, where `path.join` yields slashes). Fixtures 2/3 produced
  nothing: `only-model-is-public`, `no-circular` and
  `rpc-entry-is-the-barrel-only` do not exist in the config. A barrel
  probe (feature → `services/rpc/index.ts`) also produced nothing —
  inconclusive, same inert rule. README fixture relative paths were all
  corrected (off by depth as written; intent preserved). Orphan rule:
  only fully isolated files fire it; files with outgoing edges do not.
  Config comment + eslint message reference a non-existent
  `services/rpc/api.ts` (the barrel is `index.ts`). See §5 Q8.
- Outputs note (owner decision implemented 2026-10-10, "fix the config
  to match the map", zero package changes): forward-slash literals
  throughout; the 3 missing rules installed (`only-model-is-public`
  transcribed verbatim incl. back-refs, `no-circular`,
  `rpc-entry-is-the-barrel-only` — which REPLACES
  `no-rpc-call-outside-the-wrapper`, whose literal meaning banned the
  barrel itself); `no-supabase-outside-the-client` rescoped to
  `src/services` + direct-only (`reachable` flagged the sanctioned
  barrel chain itself); `state/ui.ts` carved out of the store rule
  (Q12); `api.ts` refs fixed. Proof re-run: exactly the 6 named
  violations, one per fixture, zero on the 91-module legit tree
  (push→barrel, session→client all silent); fixtures removed, green.
  README §4 synced same-commit (rpc row, all six fixture depths, F1
  rule name). Fixtures stay uncommitted by design — Q2 still open.
- Acceptance: Proof recorded with actual violation sets above (the six
  named violations as written are unachievable — three rules absent, five
  inert on this platform); final `npm run deps:check` is green
- Verify: `npm run deps:check` from `apps/mobile`, before and after
- Risks: `apps/mobile/README.md` §4 says "commit the config and the
  fixtures together" — permanent violation fixtures would keep every gate
  red, so proof is recorded, not committed. Unresolved tension, see §5 Q2.

