## P4 — Backend gaps (agent specifies; human DB engineer implements)

The agent never reads or writes `supabase/migrations/`. For each §13 gap
the agent delivers a **backend requirement** to the living record (see
§0): proposed RPC name following live conventions (`*_v1`, named `p_*`
params — both verified across the live catalogue), parameters, return
shape, error codes (SCREAMING_SNAKE, message-headed per §9), and grant
expectations (`SECURITY DEFINER`, least-privilege `authenticated` EXECUTE,
no direct table writes — mirroring the live-verified grant pattern:
drain RPCs service_role-only, app RPCs `authenticated`). Requirements are
explicitly **proposed, not contract** — they enter `specs-mobile/README.md`
only when a human implements, applies, probes, and retranscribes them. App
surfaces for missing write paths stay unbuilt (R-06/C rules). Each B-task
can reach `done` on a recorded, convention-checked requirement; the human
implement + apply + runtime-probe step is named in `Verify (human)` and
gates any future app task in a plan revision.

