## 3. Dependency graph (summary; `Depends on` fields are normative)

```
F-01 ─┬─▶ F-06 ──▶ C-02 ──▶ C-03 ──▶ C-04 ──┬─▶ C-06 ──▶ C-07 ──┬─▶ C-09 ──▶ P1 exit ─┬─▶ R-01 ─┬─▶ R-02 ─▶ R-03 ─▶ R-04 ─▶ R-05
      │                                     │                  │                     │                      └─▶ R-06
F-03 ─┼─▶ F-04 ─┴─▶ F-05 ──▶ C-06 ──────────┘                  │                     ├─▶ B-01 (needs R-01)
      ├─▶ F-07 ──▶ C-01 ──▶ C-05 ──▶ C-06                     │                     ├─▶ B-02 (needs C-07)
      │            └─▶ C-07 ──▶ B-04/B-02                      │                     ├─▶ B-03 (needs R-01)
      └─▶ F-08 (needs F-03,F-04,F-07)                         │                     ├─▶ B-04/B-05 (needs C-07/C-02)
                                                              │                     └─▶ S-01/S-02 (need F-01/F-06) ─▶ S-03 (needs P5 exit)
F-02: independent.  C-08: needs F-04 only.  W-01..W-04, L-01..L-03: independent (conflict note below).
```

Parallel-conflict notes: F-04/C-tasks all append to
`src/services/rpc/index.ts` + `schemas/` — sequence within P0/P1 by
dependency order, never two agents on the barrel at once. W-01 touches
`vitest.config.ts` alone (no other task edits it). S-01/S-02 both touch
`app.json` + assets — sequence S-01 before S-02. `packages/shared/src/index.ts`
is append-only via W-02; no other task edits shared. No task reads or
writes `supabase/migrations/` — ever.

## 4. Validation performed on this file

- Live database verification (read-only `SELECT`s, 2026-10-10, project
  `ACTIVE_HEALTHY`, Postgres 17): full `*_v1` catalogue read — every RPC
  this plan calls verified present with the documented args; CHECK
  vocabularies and money/total constraints match §4; 13 `settings` keys
  match §18; privilege spot-checks match §3 (`riders` SELECT=false,
  `orders` SELECT=true, addresses INSERT=false, notifications UPDATE=false;
  zero tables without RLS); drain RPCs verified service_role-only, app
  RPCs verified `authenticated`-granted; push routing returns exactly the
  7 documented rows; 19 template keys × ar/en.
- Structural check via inline Node parse (no tooling added): 38 task IDs
  unique; every `Depends on` target resolves to an existing ID or a named
  phase exit; no self-edges; graph acyclic; every task carries
  `Status/Depends/Inputs/Outputs/Acceptance/Verify`.
- Source discipline: every data claim above traces to the live checks or
  the three files. Working tree only — no git history consulted. Files
  absent from the working tree are never authority.
- Result: all checks passed at authorship. Statuses at F-02-resolution:
  F-01 `in_review` (closes on first rendered screens), F-02 `done`,
  F-03 `done`, F-04 `done`, F-05 `done`, F-06 `in_review` (photo-image
  render proof deferred to C-02, recorded in its Outputs), F-07 `done`,
  F-08 `done` (iOS plist absent — Crashlytics/Analytics on iOS recorded
  `blocked` in its Outputs; device-delivery validation stays human-side
  per its Risks); all else `pending` — no test claimed green that is
  not. Q2 (fixtures uncommitted by design) still open; Q8/Q12 resolved.

## 5. Unresolved questions (not guessed; need a human)

- Q1 Inventory target list: no in-tree file lists the intended UI
  inventory — completeness is judged against DESIGN.md §9 + the installed
  Tamagui set (F-06). Not a number, not a guess.
- Q2 Fixture proof vs green gates: `apps/mobile/README.md` §4 says commit
  the six fixtures; F-02 records proof and removes them so gates stay
  green. Confirm the deviation or amend the README (same-commit sync).
- Q3 Human-only items: §14 DB queries; P4 implement + apply + probes +
  retranscription; device observations (push, icons, splash, review
  auth); living-record location (with `CHANGELOG.md` removed, confirm
  where the record lives or designate one — no new file without asking).
- Q4 DESIGN.md scope guard: merchant-console (§1) and live-map (§10)
  sections are fully specified yet out of scope/v1 — reaffirm before any
  task cites them as build authority (this plan cites them only for
  constraints: privacy §14, sealed copy, text alternatives).
- Q5 Speed-based safety: DESIGN §14 moving lockout + stop-precondition
  timers need speed, which needs the ping RPC (out of v1). R-05 enforces
  geofence + `I AM ON FOOT` only. Confirm the reduced enforcement or
  re-scope.
- Q6 Orientation lock: `app.json` pins `"orientation": "portrait"` while
  DESIGN §§4.1/4.5 designs landscape side-by-side, tablets, and rotation
  state-preservation. Confirm portrait-lock is intentional or open it up.
- Q7 Contract-vs-live: `OPTION_SELECTION_INVALID` is listed in §15 upsert
  errors but absent from the live per-RPC census (verified); the boundary
  does not branch on it. Needs a human retranscription decision — do not
  re-add without a live re-check.
- Q8 Gate-config findings, RESOLVED 2026-10-10 per owner decision ("fix
  the config to match the map", no package changes): forward-slash
  literals throughout; `only-model-is-public`/`no-circular`/
  `rpc-entry-is-the-barrel-only` installed (back-refs proven working by
  fixture 2); `no-rpc-call-outside-the-wrapper` removed — its literal
  meaning banned the barrel §5 mandates, so the barrel-only rule carries
  its intent and the README row was replaced same-commit; supabase rule
  rescoped to `src/services` + direct-only (`reachable` flagged the
  sanctioned barrel chain); stale `api.ts` refs fixed in config + eslint
  message. The `no-orphans`-only-on-isolated-files behaviour stands as
  observed.
- Q9 Voucher failures are data, not exceptions (F-05 census 2026-10-10):
  no `VOUCHER_*` exception is raised live anywhere; voucher failures
  arrive as quote `rejections[]` rows (`QUOTE_REJECTION` vocabulary:
  `VOUCHER_UNKNOWN/EXPIRED/EXHAUSTED/MINIMUM_NOT_MET/FIRST_ORDER_ONLY/
  NOT_APPLICABLE`), handled at checkout (C-06). The behaviour layer takes
  no `VOUCHER_*` branches by intent. Specs §9 says "so are every
  `VOUCHER_*` rejection" (as raised) — needs a human retranscription
  decision, same class as Q7. Likewise `OUT_OF_STOCK` is a rejection
  code only; the mobile README §7 quote row was corrected to say so in
  the F-05 commit.
- Q10 Push language is account-side (F-08 body-read 2026-10-10):
  `register_device_token_v1` takes no language argument — it reads
  `users.preferred_language` (default `'ar'`, live-verified). "Carries the
  device's real language" is therefore a two-step path: the account
  language syncs via `update_profile_v1` (explicit user action through
  `syncLanguageAndRegister`), and registration re-reads it on upsert.
  Silent boot-time syncing was rejected (it would override an explicit
  choice). `TOKEN_ALREADY_REGISTERED` means another device holds this
  (user, role) — surfaced, never retried.
- Q11 Import style vs Metro (F-07/F-08 proof 2026-10-10): Metro resolves
  no `.js`→`.ts` substitution, so all 53 `apps/mobile` files moved to
  extensionless relative imports (recorded in `design-rules.md`);
  `packages/shared` keeps NodeNext `.js` source for its dist emit.
  Metro also honours the mobile tsconfig `@marketak/shared`→source path
  mapping (probed: default resolution lands on `src/index.ts`), so the
  mapping was removed — the app consumes `dist` like Node, tsc and
  vitest, with root `tsc --build` keeping it fresh. `expo export` passes.
- Q12 Gate-config, further, RESOLVED with Q8: `no-server-tables-in-a-store`
  carved out for `src/state/ui.ts` only (anchored path) — the map
  mandates the sign-out reset and role-switch reads there, and the rule's
  intent (no server rows in stores) is preserved for everything else.
